# p_c9d4 — Yuki's long afternoon: she is out 13:00–17:30 on weekdays

Yuki's "afternoon errands" are actually a long block: she leaves at 13:00 and returns at 17:30 on weekdays, taking her keys, jacket, sunglasses, and water bottle with her. Marco is also out (13:40–23:00), so the house is empty 13:40–17:30. The dog is taken to a neighbor or a pet-sitter during this window (dog bowl and food bag stay home but the dog is not present). On weekends Yuki is home except for a late-morning walk (10:00–11:30). Meals: 07:30 breakfast (both), 12:30 lunch (Yuki, before she leaves), 18:30 dinner (Yuki, after she returns; Marco still at work). TV: 19:30–22:00.

What sets this hypothesis apart: between 13:30 and 17:00 on a weekday, keys_yuki, jacket_yuki, sunglasses_yuki, and water_bottle_yuki are OUT_OF_HOUSE. If the robot finds any of these in the house during that window, this document is refuted. If it finds them at their resting spots (entry_table_e1, entry_floor_e1, dish_rack_k1), this document loses weight.

