# p_c4e9 — Full kit and vitamins travel; guitar on bedroom floor (fork of p_f3a7)

Two residents run a conventional two-adult household. Marco leaves for his afternoon-to-night shift around 13:40 and returns around 23:00 on weekdays; on weekends he is home except for a midday errand run (11:30–14:00). Yuki is home most of the day, taking a morning walk (07:00–08:30 weekdays, 10:00–11:30 weekends) and a shorter afternoon errand (14:30–16:00 weekdays only). The dog is fed by Yuki at 07:00 and 18:00, walked at 08:00 and 16:45. Meals are at 07:30, 12:30, and 18:30; evening TV runs 19:30–22:00. Marco bakes on weekday mornings (06:30–08:30); Yuki bakes on weekend afternoons (14:00–16:30). Marco journals at the nightstand 22:30–00:00. Yuki plays guitar 17:30–19:00 on weekdays. Marco does yoga 06:00–06:45 weekdays.

What changed from the parent (p_f3a7): Two corrections. First, the guitar's resting spot is revised from couch_l1 to bedroom_floor_b1 as the base, with the couch as a secondary daytime location. The per-object data shows the guitar at couch_l1 on only 2 of 4 sighted days, and the "worst objects" report flags three mispredictions (predicted couch, found bedroom floor). The 18:00 pass confirms the guitar is on the bedroom floor during practice. I make the bedroom floor the base resting spot and the couch a "sometimes" location during 07:00–17:00 (when Yuki may bring it to the living room for casual playing). Second, the lunchbox is corrected to stay at cupboard_k1: the per-object evidence shows 4/4 sighted days at the cupboard, 10 sightings all at cupboard_k1, and 3/3 weekday 9–17 h looks found it there with zero empty looks. Marco does not bring his lunchbox to work.

What sets this document apart from p_7a3d: between 14:00 and 23:00 on a weekday, vitamins_marco is OUT_OF_HOUSE here, while in p_7a3d it is at counter_k1. This is the key competing hypothesis: does Marco pack his vitamins for the evening at work, or does he take them at home in the evening? The per-object evidence (3/3 found at counter_k1 during 9–17 h) currently favours p_7a3d, but this document keeps the alternative alive.

